<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20962] FLR-ECRO: chmod() and utimes() block on EC file with unavailable OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20962</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;chmod()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;utimes()&lt;/tt&gt;/&lt;tt&gt;touch&lt;/tt&gt; of an EC file with a data stripe on an unavailable OST block until the OST returns.  &lt;tt&gt;chmod()&lt;/tt&gt; reaches the OSTs because the VFS sets ATTR_CTIME, which &lt;tt&gt;ll_setattr_raw()&lt;/tt&gt; sends to the objects via &lt;tt&gt;cl_setattr_ost()&lt;/tt&gt;.  See the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt; test results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;osc_io_setattr_end &amp;lt; cl_io_end &amp;lt; lov_io_end_wrapper &amp;lt; lov_io_call &amp;lt; lov_io_end &amp;lt; cl_io_end &amp;lt; cl_io_loop &amp;lt; cl_setattr_ost &amp;lt; ll_setattr_raw &amp;lt; ll_setattr &amp;lt; notify_change &amp;lt; chmod_common
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The MDS holds the authoritative timestamps, so the OST setattr of the unavailable object could be skipped or sent no-delay for an ECRO file, and repaired by &lt;tt&gt;lfs mirror resync&lt;/tt&gt; as proposed for UID/GID/PROJID in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20287" title="FLR-ECRO: change owner, group, project on degraded EC file layout" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20287"&gt;LU-20287&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
